name: os-users-retract
description: >-
  Retraction module for os-users. Removes the non-admin accounts created by
  the os-users module. The admin user removal is COMMENTED OUT by default
  because applying it fleet-wide will lock you out of every host. Uncomment
  it ONLY if you have verified an alternate access path (a different admin
  account, console access, or a backout role).

  WARNING: `state: absent` runs `userdel --remove`, which DELETES the user's
  home directory and any data in it. If you need to retain home directories
  for audit (HIPAA disposal, PCI evidence retention, etc.), archive them in
  a separate module that runs BEFORE this retraction (use depends_on).

  Removal order matters if any user owns running processes, holds file
  locks, or appears in /etc/sudoers includes. Stop services owned by these
  accounts (`systemctl stop`) before publishing this retraction.

resources:
  - name: remove-olduser
    type: user
    username: olduser
    state: absent
    # `userdel --remove` will delete /home/olduser and its contents.

  - name: remove-appuser
    type: user
    username: appuser
    state: absent
    # appuser was created with manage_home: false, so there's no /home
    # directory to remove. userdel still cleans up /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow,
    # and the per-user primary group.

  - name: remove-deploy
    type: user
    username: deploy
    state: absent
    # `userdel --remove` will delete /home/deploy and any deployment
    # artifacts cached there. Stop CI workers before applying.

  # --- DANGER: removing the admin user locks you out of every host ---
  # Uncommenting this and publishing it to the fleet will delete the `dan`
  # account, its sudoers entry, and its home directory (including
  # ~/.ssh/authorized_keys) on every machine the retraction reaches. There
  # is no automatic rollback. Only uncomment after confirming:
  #   1. An alternate admin account exists on every target host, OR
  #   2. Console / out-of-band access is available, AND
  #   3. The home directory has been archived if it contains anything you
  #      want to keep (compliance evidence, audit logs, SSH known_hosts).
  #
  # - name: remove-dan
  #   type: user
  #   username: dan
  #   state: absent
